## Concrete publication blocker found, not fixed in place

src/lumi/posttraining_checkpoint_generator_guard_v1.py:21 contains an unused
import re. Identifier/AST review confirms it is unused, has no suppression, and
is not in the historical lint baseline. Publishing this new source unchanged
would introduce F401 under the current Source CI policy.

The original file is frozen by v0.87/v0.88 hashes. It remains byte-for-byte
unchanged. No lint exemption, baseline expansion or evidence rewrite was made.
A versioned lint-only source correction and its directly affected bindings are
still required; this step does not claim the bug is fixed.

The bounded static review covered the 78 admission rows and 21 component tests.
It found no other confirmed blocker, but is not a substitute for full Ruff
0.15.1 E/F/I/B/UP checks. Ruff and a full YAML parser were unavailable locally.
The workflow's 19 exact structural tests are not a YAML-parser or Ubuntu proof.

Of the 78 admission files, 57 are tracked and 21 unpublished. The complete
publication list is not finalized: tests also require source/helper/control
dependencies beyond the native admission, including the untracked guard-source,
import-plan and runner-v2 test helpers. Do not publish only the two new entry
scripts. Source partitioning already includes new test nodes; Spark retains its
three-node scope. Neither policy needs a count-only relaxation.

